<Song resolves-to="org.jjazz.song.api.Song$SerializationProxy">
  <spVERSION>3</spVERSION>
  <spName>LadyBeGood-G-Theme</spName>
  <spComments>Oh, Lady be Good! (1924)

B y George and Ira Gershwin

Ella Fitzgerald

Intro:
Listen to my tale of woe,
it&apos;s terribly sad but true,
All dressed up, no place to go
Each evening I&apos;m awfully blue.
I must win some handsome guy
Can&apos;t go on like this,
I could blossom out I know,
With somebody just like you. So...

Oh, sweet and lovely lady, be good
Oh, lady, be good to me
I am so awfully misunderstood
So lady, be good to me

Oh, please have some pity
I&apos;m all alone in this big city

I tell you I&apos;m just a lonesome babe in the wood,
So lady be good to me.

Oh, please have some pity
I&apos;m all alone in this big city

I tell you I&apos;m just a lonesome babe in the wood,
So lady be good to me.

Oh lady be good to me.</spComments>
  <spTempo>180</spTempo>
  <spTags/>
